<title>USA: Genzyme sells identity-testing assets.</title>
<headline>Genzyme sells identity-testing assets.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Mass. 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Genzyme Corp's general division said on Friday it sold the primary assets of its identity-testing services laboratory to Laboratory Corp of America Holdings for an undisclosed sum.</p>
<p>The unit, called Genetic Design Inc, would continue to develop and market medical genetic testing services, the company said.  </p>
<p>The company said the sale was part of its plan to focus on its genetics business. &quot;We believe medical genetic testing will be an important growth sector in the future,&quot; said Henri Termeer, chairman and chief executive officer.</p>
<p>For the nine months ending September 30, Genetic Design had revenues of $10.4 million, the company said.</p>
<p>Genzyme said the acquisition complemented LabCorp's paternity testing operation in North Carolina.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
